#====================================================================
# DRAFT-util-linux-login-2.42.2-ohos-musl-pam-portability
# — util-linux-login 2.42.2 OHOS musl/PAM portability closed loop
# 触发事件: PR #7031, CI #37390
# 查重: E245(vhangup syscall shim), E534(musl GNU extensions), E467(AutotoolsDeps)
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-util-linux-login-2.42.2-ohos-musl-pam-portability
trigger_tool:           conan|configure|clang|ld|test
phase:                  configuration|compilation|linking|testing
error_signature:        security/pam_appl.h.*no|
                         checking for GNU utmpx functions... no|
                         call to undeclared function 'getusershell'|
                         incompatible integer to pointer conversion|
                         undefined symbol: getutxent|
                         undefined symbol: getutxid|
                         undefined symbol: getutxline|
                         undefined symbol: pututxline|
                         undefined symbol: setutxent|
                         undefined symbol: endutxent|
                         undefined symbol: utmpxname|
                         undefined symbol: vhangup|
                         Read timed out

severity:               2
category:               autotools|conan|musl|pam|portability
match_keywords:         util-linux-login, util-linux 2.42.2, linux-pam,
                         AutotoolsDeps, CPPFLAGS, security/pam_appl.h,
                         GNU utmpx, getutxent, pututxline, utmpxname,
                         vhangup, getusershell, shells.h, OHOS musl,
                         focused Conan package, mirror fallback
title:                  util-linux login 2.42.2 on OHOS: focused Conan subpackage with PAM discovery and musl utmpx/shell compatibility

root_cause: >
  1) util-linux's configure requirements make login depend on PAM headers and
  GNU utmpx capability. Conan's dependency include paths must reach autoconf
  preprocess probes through CPPFLAGS; putting them only in CFLAGS is not
  enough for AC_CHECK_HEADERS(security/pam_appl.h). 2) OHOS musl declares
  utmpx types but does not export the getutx*/pututxline/utmpxname
  implementations, and it does not provide vhangup. Declarations alone solve
  compilation but leave undefined symbols at link time. 3) OHOS musl neither
  declares nor implements the getusershell family. util-linux's shells.h is
  included by login.c only when HAVE_LIBECONF and USE_VENDORDIR are enabled,
  so definitions in lib/shells.c do not automatically make prototypes visible
  in the non-libeconf path; implicit int becomes char* conversion failure.
  4) configure rejects login when GNU utmpx extensions are absent even though
  the focused login package can degrade accounting paths safely for this CI
  scope. 5) The official kernel.org endpoint can time out on a CI worker.
affected_scope: >
  Focused util-linux subpackages or comparable autotools applications that
  enable only selected programs on OHOS musl and depend on Conan-hosted PAM.
  The getusershell section applies when a source file calls the family but
  only conditionally includes the project header carrying its prototypes.
  It does not claim full interactive login runtime coverage.
verification_cmd: >
  git apply --check patches/*.patch;
  CI_PACKAGES="archives/u/util-linux-login/2.42.2" zsh ci/conan/build_and_test.sh;
  inspect CI log for Conan build, test_package, L0 and L1 results.

rec_priority:            1
rec_approach:            focused-autotools-pam-musl-compat
rec_description: >
  Build only login/nologin, generate linux-pam paths with AutotoolsDeps,
  permit login without GNU utmpx, guard updwtmpx, define missing no-op
  utmpx/vhangup symbols under !__GLIBC__, and make getusershell prototypes
  visible while providing NULL-returning definitions in lib/shells.c.
rec_command: >
  conan create archives/u/util-linux-login/2.42.2
  --profile:build=default --profile:host=ohos-aarch64
rec_auto_fix:            true
rec_impl:                patch-files

fallback_priority:       2
fallback_approach:       consult-existing-knowledge
fallback_description: >
  If real terminal hangup semantics are required, follow E245 and preserve
  vhangup through the available syscall instead of treating this CI-focused
  no-op link stub as the final runtime implementation.
fallback_command:        grep -R "SYS_vhangup" "$SYSROOT/usr/include"
fallback_auto_fix:       false
fallback_impl:           none

forbid_1_pattern:        #ifdef\s+__OHOS__|#if\s+defined\(__OHOS__\)
forbid_1_reason:         CI showed the OHOS clang target does not define __OHOS__, so such guards silently omit the compatibility code.
forbid_1_consequence:    The same undefined-symbol errors remain on the OHOS CI worker.

forbid_2_pattern:        disable-all-programs.*enable-all-programs|build.*complete util-linux suite.*for login
forbid_2_reason:         The reusable packaging boundary is a focused login/nologin Conan application, not the full util-linux suite.
forbid_2_consequence:    Unrelated programs and optional system dependencies widen the adaptation and CI failure surface.

forbid_3_pattern:        100%.*0/0|pass rate.*0/0.*100%
forbid_3_reason:         The upstream package-level test denominator is zero and must be reported as not applicable.
forbid_3_consequence:    A fabricated upstream pass rate makes the Path B evidence invalid.

principles:              P001, P003, P011
caused_by:
similar_to:              E245, E467, E534
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of:

